      "description": "A simple litter system model using the euler method. Carbon storage C is calculated in dependency of litter fall rate (Cinput) and rate constant for litter loss (Closs) as:&lt;br/&gt;C(t + 1) = C(t) + (Cinput - Closs * C(t)) * dt&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Typical values:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;- Tropical Rainforest:&lt;br/&gt;-- Litter fall rate: 500 [g/m&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;/a]&lt;br/&gt;-- Litter loss rate: 2.0 [1/a]&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;- Temperate forest:&lt;br/&gt;-- Litter fall rate: 240 [g/m&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;/a]&lt;br/&gt;-- Litter loss rate: 0.4 [1/a]&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;- Boreal forest:&lt;br/&gt;-- Litter fall rate: 50 [g/m&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;/a]&lt;br/&gt;-- Litter loss rate: 0.05 [1/a]&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Reference:&lt;br/&gt;Hugget, R.J. (1993): 'Modelling the Human Impact on Nature', Oxford University Press.&lt;br/&gt;",
