        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "SAGA.ta_slope_stability.5",
      "title": "ANGMAP",
      "description": "&lt;br/&gt;This tool computes the acute angle raster between the topographic surface defined by slope and aspect rasters internally derived from input elevation raster, and a structural plane defined by diop direction- and dip grids. Optionally, the dip direction and dip of the cutting line linears between the two planes can be calculated&lt;br/&gt;Reference: &lt;a href=\"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0098300403000864\"&gt;G&uuml;nther, A. (2003). SLOPEMAP: programs for automated mapping of geometrical and kinematical properties of hard rock hill slopes. Computers & Geosciences, 29, 865 - 875&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;",
